views.help=()=>{
  const c=mmCount();
  return`<h2>Help &amp; User Manual</h2>
<div class="card">
  <h3>Welcome</h3>
  <p><b>IT-Tech Consulting – Business Manager</b> is a browser-based app for running an IT services business: clients, jobs, a calendar, quotes, invoices, stock, projects and accounting. It has <b>${c.pages}</b> pages in <b>${c.sections}</b> sections. All data is stored in this browser (<code>localStorage</code>); no server is needed for normal use.</p>
  <div class="row">
    <button class="p f0" data-hp="mindmap">Open site mindmap</button>
    <button class="f0" id="hp_csv">Download mindmap CSV</button>
    <button class="f0" data-hp="cal">Open Calendar</button>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="card">
  <h3>1. Quick start</h3>
  <ol>
    <li><b>Settings &amp; data</b> – set company name, address, VAT, bank details, default terms and hourly rates.</li>
    <li><b>Appearance</b> – choose theme, layout (side / top nav) and currency format (ZAR, USD, etc.).</li>
    <li><b>Clients &amp; Accounts</b> – add your first client.</li>
    <li><b>Business Breakdown / Pricing</b> – confirm or edit the service catalogue prices.</li>
    <li>Create a <b>Quotation</b> → mark Accepted → convert to <b>Invoice</b> or <b>Project</b>.</li>
    <li>Add <b>Jobs</b> with due dates and watch them appear on the <b>Calendar</b>. Log time in <b>Projects</b> or <b>Workspace</b> and record expenses in the <b>Financial log</b>.</li>
  </ol>
</div>

<div class="card">
  <h3>2. Operations &amp; CRM</h3>
  <ul>
    <li><b>Dashboard</b> – money in/out, open quotes, debtors, project health and the next 7 days from the calendar.</li>
    <li><b>Clients &amp; Accounts</b> – master client list; open a client for related jobs and documents. Set a <i>next review</i> date and it appears on the Calendar.</li>
    <li><b>Leads &amp; Pipeline</b> – drag deals across stages; create a quote or project from a won deal. Expected close dates appear on the Calendar.</li>
    <li><b>Jobs &amp; Work Orders</b> – schedule work, set priority, link to projects, log notes. The due date places the job on the Calendar.</li>
    <li><b>Field Dispatches</b> – call-outs and urgent work; shown in red on the Calendar.</li>
    <li><b>Vendors &amp; Suppliers / Directory</b> – people and companies you buy from or subcontract to.</li>
    <li><b>Service Directory</b> – the catalogue of services and packages you can add to quotations.</li>
  </ul>
</div>

<div class="card" id="help_cal">
  <h3>3. Calendar</h3>
  <ul>
    <li><b>Views</b> – Day, Week, Month and Year. Use ‹ and › to move by one day, week, month or year; <b>Today</b> jumps back. Weeks start on Monday. Your chosen view is remembered.</li>
    <li><b>Click a day</b> (or Tab to it and press Enter) to open the <b>Day detail</b> panel below the calendar. It lists everything on that date with an <b>Open</b> button for each item, and has a <b>diary note</b> (type, title, priority, all-day or start/end time, location, people, notes). There is one note per day; saving an empty note removes it.</li>
    <li><b>What appears</b> – job and dispatch due dates, project start/end/review dates and milestones, deals (expected close), client account reviews, invoices (issued and due), quotations (and expiry), purchase orders, RFQs (and needed-by), shipments (and ETA), asset and device warranties, stock movements, bank and ledger lines, and your day notes.</li>
    <li><b>Filters</b> – tick or untick Jobs, Projects, CRM, Finance, Shipping, Notes and Assets / IoT / Stock. <b>Show completed</b> controls finished items (done jobs, paid invoices, closed quotes, received POs, delivered shipments, completed projects and milestones, won or lost deals). Filters are remembered.</li>
    <li><b>Colours</b> – red: urgent dispatches, due invoices, ending warranties and needed-by dates; amber: reviews, expiries and ETAs; green: completed; purple: projects; blue: deals and shipments; grey: day notes.</li>
    <li><b>Quick create</b> – <b>New job this day</b> and <b>Dispatch this day</b> open the job form with that due date filled in.</li>
    <li><b>Phones</b> – the month grid shows coloured bars instead of text; tap a day to read its items.</li>
    <li><b>Elsewhere</b> – the Dashboard lists the next 7 days, Ctrl+K search finds calendar notes, and <b>Workspace → Calendar</b> shows jobs only.</li>
  </ul>
</div>

<div class="card">
  <h3>4. Sales, stock &amp; billing</h3>
  <ul>
    <li><b>Quotations</b> – line items from the catalogue or free text; send, accept, decline; convert to invoice or project.</li>
    <li><b>Invoices</b> – record payments; print or view statements per client.</li>
    <li><b>Purchase Orders</b> – order parts from suppliers; receiving can feed inventory and project costs.</li>
    <li><b>Procurement &amp; RFQs</b> – request supplier quotes and convert an RFQ to a PO.</li>
    <li><b>Inventory &amp; Warehousing</b> – stock levels, movements and reorder points.</li>
    <li><b>Shipping &amp; Fulfillment</b> – shipments, status and ETAs.</li>
    <li><b>Hardware Lifecycle</b> – register hardware, track warranties and send it to Fixed Assets.</li>
    <li><b>Pricing Configurations</b> – rate cards and packages (backed by the catalogue in Business Breakdown).</li>
  </ul>
</div>

<div class="card">
  <h3>5. Projects &amp; time</h3>
  <ul>
    <li><b>Projects Dashboard</b> – create projects (blank or from template / accepted quote / won deal). Tabs: Overview, Tasks, Timeline (Gantt + milestones), Time, Costs, Billing, Risks, Docs, Team.</li>
    <li><b>Project Workflow Wizard</b> – a guided five-phase path: Initiation, Planning, Execution, Monitoring &amp; Controlling, Closure.</li>
    <li><b>Workspace</b> – list, kanban, calendar or Gantt across all jobs; task dependencies block “Done” until upstream is finished.</li>
    <li><b>Timesheets</b> – timers and manual hours; bill unbilled time from the project Billing tab.</li>
    <li><b>Capacity</b> – compare remaining open hours to weekly capacity (set in Settings).</li>
    <li><b>Installation Pipelines / IoT Nodes</b> – guided deployment workflow and device tracking.</li>
  </ul>
</div>

<div class="card">
  <h3>6. Money &amp; reports</h3>
  <ul>
    <li><b>Accounting Core</b> – income vs expenses, VAT summary, rough tax set-aside.</li>
    <li><b>Financial log (Expenses)</b> – daybook of income/expense lines; can tag a project.</li>
    <li><b>Banking &amp; Reconciliation</b> – log bank transactions and reconcile them with open invoices.</li>
    <li><b>General Ledger / Tax Center / Fixed Assets / Cash Forecast</b> – deeper books, tax views, asset register and a 13-week cash view.</li>
    <li><b>Reports</b> – pick a report type and date range, or type a question such as “vat last month” or “sales by client this year”.</li>
    <li><b>Audit log</b> – recent changes for governance.</li>
  </ul>
</div>

<div class="card">
  <h3>7. Administration</h3>
  <ul>
    <li><b>Side panel modules</b> – switch modules on or off; presets for all, optional off or core only. <b>Side panel modules</b> and <b>System Backups &amp; Governance</b> are always visible and cannot be hidden.</li>
    <li><b>User Roles &amp; Permissions</b> – assign a role to people in the Directory and apply a role as a side-panel preset. Applying a role as a preset shows only that role’s modules in this browser’s side panel.</li>
    <li><b>Custom Fields &amp; Templates</b> – add fields to records and edit the quotation and invoice print templates.</li>
    <li><b>Integrations &amp; APIs / Local Folder &amp; Data Sync</b> – export hub and file or network backups.</li>
  </ul>
</div>

<div class="card">
  <h3>8. Data safety</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>Data stays in <b>this browser only</b>. Clearing site data will erase it.</li>
    <li>Use <b>Settings → download full backup</b> (JSON) regularly and store the file somewhere safe. Backups include your calendar notes and filter choices.</li>
    <li><b>Local Folder &amp; Data Sync</b> can help keep a file copy if your browser supports it.</li>
    <li>Excel/CSV export on lists and reports is available where the download buttons appear (Excel needs internet for the SheetJS library).</li>
  </ul>
</div>

<div class="card">
  <h3>9. Search, shortcuts &amp; tips</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>Press <b>Ctrl+K</b> (⌘K on a Mac) or use the Search button to find clients, quotes, invoices, jobs, projects, deals, suppliers, stock, ledger lines, RFQs, shipments, calendar notes and pages.</li>
    <li>Use the side panel (or top nav on small screens) to move between modules.</li>
    <li>Print-friendly documents use the hidden <code>#doc</code> area – use the Print buttons on quotes, invoices, statements and project status reports.</li>
    <li>Currency symbol and number format are under <b>Appearance</b>; amounts are not auto-converted when you change currency.</li>
  </ul>
</div>

<div class="card">
  <h3>10. Module reference</h3>
  <p class="mu">Every page, generated from the live module list.</p>
  ${NAV_CATALOG.map(([sec,items])=>`<h4 style="margin:12px 0 4px">${esc(sec)}</h4><ul>${items.map(([id,label])=>`<li><a href="#" data-hp="${id}"><b>${esc(label)}</b></a>${navOn(id)?"":` <span class="tag">off</span>`} – ${esc(MOD_INFO[id]||"")}</li>`).join("")}</ul>`).join("")}
</div>

<div class="card">
  <h3>11. Support map</h3>
  <p>For a tree of every menu item with descriptions and related modules, open the mindmap page or download it as CSV.</p>
  <div class="row"><button class="p f0" id="hp_csv2">Download site-mindmap.csv</button><button class="f0" data-hp="mindmap">View mindmap page</button></div>
  <p class="mu" style="margin-top:10px">Sections: ${NAV_CATALOG.map(s=>esc(s[0])).join(", ")}. Contact your administrator if this copy was customised for your company.</p>
</div>`;
};
